  "published": "2026-10-29T08:13:42.33Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking: Redis sessions are encrypted directly with jose-jwt using PBES2-HS256+A128KW and A256GCM. Bff:EncryptionKey is required. Session payloads are bound to their Redis key. Framework cookies, OIDC state and antiforgery retain an encrypted shared key ring in Redis. Stop old replicas, choose a new Bff:KeyNamespace and require users to sign in again. See the session migration guide.",
